Name: LemurX luakit-compatible Lua runtime
URL: (first-party, see //LICENSE)
Version: 1
License: BSD-3-Clause
License File: //LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: yes

Description:
A from-scratch, API-compatible re-implementation of the luakit browser's Lua
surface for Chromium/Android:

  kernel/   the object model (signals, properties), widget tree, webview,
            timers, ipc_channel, soup, sqlite3, regex, lfs, xdg, msg,
            stylesheets, downloads, unique-instance, custom schemes, plus the
            renderer-side (web/) dom_document, page, ipc, luakit modules.
  lib/      the standard luakit module set (window, webview, modes, binds,
            lousy.*, chrome pages, adblock, follow, formfiller, session, ...)
            rewritten clean-room from luakit's public API documentation.
  config/   default rc.lua / theme.lua.

No luakit source code (C or Lua) is included; the only inheritance is the
public Lua API (names, signatures, signal names, settings keys) so that
scripts written against luakit's documentation keep working.

Everything under this directory is BSD-3-Clause, the same as the rest of
LemurX. Regenerate luakit_assets.gni after adding/removing files:
  cd chrome/lemurx/luakit && ./gen_assets_gni.sh
